{"title":"-base accepts a branch name; merge-base command never shown, so wrong base gives silent wrong holds","severity":"P2","file":"review-triage/tools/lineorigin/README.md","line":40,"confidence":50,"autofix_class":"manual","owner":"downstream-resolver","requires_verification":false,"pre_existing":false,"suggested_fix":"README -base row: pass the SHA of git merge-base <branch> HEAD, not a branch name; add that command to premise-check.md routes 2/3."},
{"title":"Tool treats dirty target file as unverifiable for every -rev, spec scopes it to result-file reviews","severity":"P3","file":"review-triage/tools/lineorigin/lineorigin.go","line":89,"confidence":50,"autofix_class":"advisory","owner":"human","requires_verification":false,"pre_existing":false,"suggested_fix":"State in premise-check.md that the dirty-file check applies to every -rev."},
{"title":"Retry instruction unbounded; result->D8 mapping and multi-range aggregation implicit","severity":"P3","file":"review-triage/skills/review-triage/references/premise-check.md","line":119,"confidence":50,"autofix_class":"advisory","owner":"downstream-resolver","requires_verification":false,"pre_existing":false,"suggested_fix":"Add: fix only mis-copied values, at most one rerun; one sentence mapping holds -> go on to (2), not-holds/unverifiable -> 当たらない; for non-contiguous lines run per range and combine."}
