{"title":"Inherited GIT_DIR / GIT_INDEX_FILE / replace-object env can redirect the git calls away from -root","severity":"P3","file":"review-triage/tools/lineorigin/lineorigin.go","line":490,"confidence":50,"autofix_class":"gated_auto","owner":"downstream-resolver","requires_verification":true,"pre_existing":false,"suggested_fix":"Build cmd.Env by dropping GIT_DIR, GIT_WORK_TREE, GIT_INDEX_FILE, GIT_COMMON_DIR, GIT_NAMESPACE, GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY and GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES from os.Environ(), and add GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1."},
{"title":"skip-worktree / assume-unchanged hide an uncommitted edit, so -rev mode reports holds instead of unverifiable","severity":"P3","file":"review-triage/tools/lineorigin/lineorigin.go","line":533,"confidence":50,"autofix_class":"advisory","owner":"human","requires_verification":false,"pre_existing":false,"suggested_fix":"Before the diff, run git ls-files -v -- <file> and treat tag h (assume-unchanged) or S/s (skip-worktree) as unverifiable, or compare the worktree file against git show HEAD:<file> directly."}
],"residual_risks":["Identical-line ambiguity: blame decides which of several identical lines is the added one, so a finding on the other copy can get a wrong holds or not-holds. Inherent to line-based blame.","README says git >= 2.23, but rev-parse --end-of-options needs about 2.30; older git fails loudly (exit 2).","exists() turns any cat-file failure into false (safe direction for D8).","Filenames with embedded newlines are printed raw in the rename-case note, so a hostile repo could inject extra result: lines."],"testing_gaps":["No test with a textconv diff driver configured.","No test with GIT_DIR / GIT_INDEX_FILE / GIT_WORK_TREE in the environment, or with a replace ref.","No test for skip-worktree / assume-unchanged on the -rev guard.","No README limitation entry for duplicate-line insertion ambiguity."]},
